You are helping build **Lexicon**, a daily vocabulary practice app (React 18 + TypeScript + Vite + Tailwind + Framer Motion + Zustand + Tauri v2).

## Read before coding

- @CLAUDE.md — canonical AI instructions
- @CONTINUING.md — current state, design principles, common changes
- @ROADMAP.md — phased plan with priorities; consult before proposing new work
- @CHANGELOG.md — shipped features per release
- @README.md — user-facing overview
- @src/types/index.ts — domain contract

## Non-negotiable conventions

- Pure logic in `src/lib/`, state in `src/store/`, UI in `src/components/` and `src/pages/`.
- Zustand stores are the source of truth. Never touch `localStorage` directly outside the three stores.
- Progress records are keyed by `wordId` and must survive vocab reloads.
- Framer Motion easing is `[0.16, 1, 0.3, 1]` throughout.
- The word itself uses `display-serif` (Fraunces). Body text uses Inter. Numbers use `tabular`.
- Colors are HSL CSS variables in `src/styles/globals.css`. Never hardcode.

## When adding a new page

1. Create `src/pages/NewPage.tsx`
2. Add to the `Page` union in `src/store/useAppStore.ts`
3. Register in the `renderPage` switch in `src/App.tsx`
4. Add a nav entry in `src/components/Sidebar.tsx`

## Before reporting done

Run `npm run typecheck && npm run build`. Both must pass.
